KZ2 patch 2121: a D3D12 WARP fallback, so kz2.exe starts on a machine with no GPU (the Windows VM
installer test). from Killzone 3 PC port patch 2099 (2099-mouse-sensitivity-look-accumulator-d3d12-warp.patch, its
D3D12 part only: rsx_d3d12_device.h and the two device sites; same author, MIT). The mouse part of KZ3's 2099 is not
taken.
libs/video/rsx_d3d12_device.h (new): rsx_d3d12_create_device: the default adapter as before, WARP
(IDXGIFactory4::EnumWarpAdapter) only when that gives no device, RSX_D3D12_WARP=1 forces WARP, =0 never; one
"[d3d12] device" line per device (adapter, vendor, device, flags, software, max feature level, binding tier, highest
shader model).
KZ2 change for KZ3's VM finding (the WARP adapter "Microsoft Basic Render Driver" reported software=0, its
DXGI_ADAPTER_FLAG_SOFTWARE missing): rsx_adapter_is_software() also knows it by vendor 0x1414 / device 0x008C. The
backend's high-performance adapter loop skips it (so it is never taken as the hardware adapter), and the log line
says software=1 for it.
Public issue #13: the live renderer got the iGPU on a hybrid laptop (D3D12CreateDevice(NULL) = the default
adapter). rsx_d3d12_create_device now enumerates with IDXGIFactory6::EnumAdapterByGpuPreference(HIGH_PERFORMANCE), skips
software adapters, tries each (HRESULT logged), then the default adapter, then WARP; adapters and the chosen LUID are
logged; rsx_pick_device is the pure order logic (host test). KZ3 makes the same fix, credit mutual.
rsx_d3d12_backend.c and rsx_live_draw.c create their device through it. The hardware path is unchanged: a GPU
adapter is picked by the same loop and the same D3D12CreateDevice(NULL) as before. Host test
tools/runtime/test_d3d12_warp.sh. KZ2 test value RSX_D3D12_WARP=fail: no device at all, for the no-device exit of
port/kz2/main.cpp under Proton (whose DXGI always answers with the hardware adapter).

